### Phase 2 implementation and verification

- Rule contract -> Phase 1 placement-validation decisions + `../vsapi/Common/Collectible/Block/Block.cs:CanPlaceBlock` -> `IBrushPlacementValidator` and `PlayerBrushPlacementValidator` at their planned module paths. The adapter keeps non-null world/player references private and directly forwards native virtual dispatch and the failure-code reference; claims, collision and behavior rules are not reimplemented.
- Brush decision routing -> `BuildBrushInstance.ResolveFinalSelectionPosition/TryGetValidSnappedPosition/TryUpdatePlacementValidity` and the original selection builder -> internal `src/BuildBrush/Placement/BrushPlacementValidation.cs`. It owns the existing snapped/fallback search and selection cloning so the same production decisions can be tested without player-dependent construction. Existing instance methods remain facades binding this rule context; validity/entity assignment and missing-block/position guards stay on the brush.
- Composition -> both controller brush-creation sites bind the actual world/player once per brush. The original two-argument brush constructor remains available and uses native validation; a three-argument overload accepts an explicit validator. Controllers still acquire player state in this intermediate implementation; their narrow-input construction and moving composition fully to the systems remain Phase 3 work.
- Focused evidence -> `VanillaBuildingExpanded.Tests/BuildBrush/BrushPlacementValidationTests.cs` -> eleven passing cases exercise accepted snapping, rejected snapping with accepted/rejected fallback, coincident-candidate call order, null-block semantics, rejected preview validation, cloned face/hit/selection-box data, source mutation isolation, fresh failure codes, and missing dependencies. These are decision tests of the extracted production component, not native claims/collision integration or a migrated player-independent brush constructor.
- Final delegated build/test receipt -> `C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Temp\vbe-player-dependencies-phase2-20261023-074046` (`focused-final.log/.trx`, `full-final.log/.trx`, `summary.json`, `candidate-hashes.json`). With process-local `NUGET_PACKAGES=C:\Users\Sisco\.nuget\packages`, `dotnet test VanillaBuildingExpanded.Tests/VanillaBuildingExpanded.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter "FullyQualifiedName~BrushPlacementValidationTests|FullyQualifiedName~BrushSnappingTests"` plus TRX output passed 52/52 (11 placement + 41 snapping). The subsequent full project run with `--no-build --no-restore` passed 170 and failed 189 of 359, zero skipped. All failures retain the existing missing-method proxy signature: 187 `IPlayer`, two `IServerPlayer`; no unrelated failures. Build: zero errors, 31 compiler warnings, no NuGet warnings.
- Environment -> SDK `10.0.401`, runtime `10.0.13`, API assembly `1.22.7.0`; installed API hash unchanged from Phase 1. No mock-tool/API patch, package, game launch or live-runtime evidence is part of this increment. Inherited architecture constraints were reconciled against current source; the previously identified stale ack/seq wording remains Phase 5 documentation work.

